{
  "title": "About SemIndex Plugin",
  "story": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "5089c35d04cdad90",
      "text": "The SemIndex plugin is the farm's semantic-index WRITER. It embeds every page of every site in the farm (BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5, 384-dim) in a supervised background child process and writes each site's semantic-vectors.json \u2014 so federated semantic search works with no Python, no FastAPI, and no external indexer. The [[About Similarity Plugin]] is the matching reader; install both for fully local search."
    },
    {
      "type": "semindex",
      "id": "fa8383bc59188fc4",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "7ea58be9f3ded594",
      "text": "# Routes\n\n- GET /system/semindex-status.json \u2014 build, queue and model-download status (polled by the widget above)\n- GET|POST /system/semindex-build.json?domains=glob&force=1 \u2014 enqueue builds, owner or admin only\n- GET|POST /system/semindex-embed.json \u2014 embed one text (`?text=\u2026` or `{text}`); a remote slim Similarity can point WIKI_EMBED_URL here"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "fd5c947526d0693b",
      "text": "# Configuration\n\nEnvironment variables, all optional:\n\n- WIKI_SEMINDEX_MODE \u2014 off | query-only | writer (default writer). One writer per synced farm: keep mirrors on query-only.\n- WIKI_SEMINDEX_SCAN_MS \u2014 freshness scan interval (default 10 min)\n- WIKI_SEMINDEX_SETTLE_MS \u2014 quiet period after edits before rebuilding (default 5 min)\n- WIKI_SEMINDEX_THROTTLE_MS \u2014 pause between page embeds (default 50)\n- WIKI_SEMINDEX_IDLE_MS \u2014 embedder idle timeout before the model's memory is released (default 10 min)\n- WIKI_SEMINDEX_MIN_PAGES \u2014 skip sites smaller than this (default 1)\n- WIKI_MODEL_CACHE \u2014 model download cache (default ~/.cache/wiki-semindex, ~130MB on first run)\n- WIKI_EMBED_FORCE_WASM=1 \u2014 force the WASM backend (automatic on musl/Alpine)\n- WIKI_EMBED_QUANTIZED=1 \u2014 int8 model (~34MB) for low-memory servers\n- WIKI_SEMINDEX_MAINTENANCE=1 \u2014 write a .semindex/maintenance.json flag during builds for a security-module maintenance gate\n- WIKI_SEMINDEX_TIMEOUT_MS \u2014 per-embed timeout (default 5 min)\n- WIKI_EMBED_CHILD_HEAP_MB \u2014 embed child V8 heap cap (default 512)\n- WIKI_EMBED_MAX_CRASHES / WIKI_EMBED_CRASH_WINDOW_MS / WIKI_EMBED_COOLDOWN_MS \u2014 circuit breaker: crashes tolerated per window (default 3 / 10 min) before embedding pauses for the cooldown (default 5 min)"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "827ea31bca31c963",
      "text": "**Version:** 0.2.3\n\nSince 0.2.0 the embedder runs in a supervised child process rather than a worker thread, so a fatal error in the ONNX runtime (abort, out-of-memory, bad model file) can never take down the wiki server: it fails that one embed, and repeated crashes trip a circuit breaker that pauses indexing while it cools down. Same isolation strategy as the Similarity plugin 0.9.0.\n\n0.2.3 adds POST to the embed route, so it can serve as a remote farm's `WIKI_EMBED_URL`. That matters because this route is rate-limited (a per-IP token bucket) where Similarity's own `/system/embed.json` is not \u2014 a public name needs the limited one."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "82915075ee65a796",
      "text": "# Repositories\n\n- [https://github.com/Hitchhikers-Guide-to-the-Galaxy/wiki-plugin-semindex github]\n- [https://www.npmjs.com/package/wiki-plugin-semindex npm]"
    }
  ],
